# T-1034: [do result ...] with explicit Result monad specifier — single-step form.
# Uses bare Ok constructor (injected as Result.Ok at desugar time, visible after T-1048).
# NOTE: The inferred-specifier path ([do [Result.Ok 42]] without explicit "result")
# is not yet exercised here; that scenario requires resolve_monad_from_surface to
# pick up the monad identity from a qualified DotAccess like Result.Ok, and is
# deferred until the qualified constructor form is reliably accessible end-to-end.
# This test covers the explicit-specifier + bare-constructor path.
[do result [Ok value: 42]]
=== out
Variant(Result.Ok, Int(42))

=== warn
[UndefinedVariable] undefined variable: Ok
